d":true,"correct":true,"rows":2,"expected_rows":2,"error":""},{"question_id":"h06","backend":"claude","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","question":"How many cases were opened within 7 days (inclusive) after the telemetry failure date of the drive linked to the case's asset?","attempts":1,"executed":true,"correct":true,"rows":1,"expected_rows":1,"error":""},{"question_id":"h07","backend":"claude","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","question":"Which users ran logged queries against tables that are derived, at any depth, from telemetry_daily? Return user_name and the number of such queries, highest first.","attempts":2,"executed":true,"correct":true,"rows":6,"expected_rows":6,"error":""},{"question_id":"h08","backend":"claude","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","question":"Which data products include a table that has a column meaning the glossary term 'Service Failure (support)'? Return the data product names.","attempts":1,"executed":true,"correct":true,"rows":1,"expected_rows":1,"error":""},{"question_id":"h09","backend":"claude","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","question":"How many distinct suppliers are the preferred supplier of a part used by a product that is installed at a site of the resolved account ACC-00148?","attempts":1,"executed":true,"correct":true,"rows":1,"expected_rows":1,"error":""},{"question_id":"h10","backend":"claude","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","question":"Which vault has the most drives with a telemetry failure sitting in pods flagged risky? Return the vault key and that count.","attempts":1,"executed":true,"correct":true,"rows":1,"expected_rows":1,"error":""}]},"trust":{"now":{"run_id":"20261017T091138-now","as_of":"2026-10-17T09:11:38.888028+00:00","checks":111,"by_status":{"pass":104,"fail":7,"skip":0},"summary":{"fleet_health":{"status":"fail","checks":32,"failed":1,"failed_checks":["freshness:drive_summary.last_seen"],"newest_event":"2026-06-30"},"parts_demand":{"status":"fail","checks":38,"failed":1,"failed_checks":["freshness:dispatch.scheduled_at"],"newest_event":"2026-07-11T11:18:32"},"dispatch_quality":{"status":"fail","checks":38,"failed":2,"failed_checks":["freshness:case.opened_at","freshness:dispatch.scheduled_at"],"newest_event":"2026-07-11T11:18:32"}},"by_kind":[{"kind":"completeness","pass":76,"fail":0,"skip":0},{"kind":"freshness","pass":0,"fail":4,"skip":0},{"kind":"schema_drift","pass":28,"fail":0,"skip":0},{"kind":"summary","pass":0,"fail":3,"skip":0}],"failed":[{"data_product":"fleet_health","check":"freshness","table":"drive_summary.last_seen","status":"fail","threshold":24,"value":2625.2},{"data_product":"fleet_health","check":"summary","table":null,"status":"fail","threshold":0,"value":1},{"data_product":"parts_demand","check":"freshness","table":"dispatch.scheduled_at","status":"fail","threshold":168,"value":2349.9},{"data_product":"parts_demand","check":"summary","table":null,"status":"fail","threshold":0,"value":1},{"data_product":"dispatch_quality","check":"freshness","table":"case.opened_at","status":"fail","threshold":24,"value":2529.9},{"data_product":"dispatch_quality","check":"freshness","table":"dispatch.scheduled_at","status":"fail","threshold":24,"value":2349.9},{"data_product":"dispatch_quality","check":"summary","table":null,"status":"fail","threshold":0,"value":2}]},"asof":{"run_id":"20260701T000000-asof","as_of":"2026-07-01T00:00:00+00:00","checks":111,"by_status":{"pass":111,"fail":0,"skip":0},"summary":{"fleet_health":{"status":"pass","checks":32,"failed":0,"failed_checks":[],"newest_event":"2026-06-30"},"parts_demand":{"status":"pass","checks":38,"failed":0,"failed_checks":[],"newest_event":"2026-07-11T11:18:32"},"dispatch_quality":{"status":"pass","checks":38,"failed":0,"failed_checks":[],"newest_event":"2026-07-11T11:18:32"}},"by_kind":[{"kind":"completeness","pass":76,"fail":0,"skip":0},{"kind":"freshness","pass":4,"fail":0,"skip":0},{"kind":"schema_drift","pass":28,"fail":0,"skip":0},{"kind":"summary","pass":3,"fail":0,"skip":0}],"failed":[]}},"lineage_example":{"command":"uv run python -m ekg.lineage provenance reports/fleet_risk_sites.csv expected_failures_30d","output":"reports/fleet_risk_sites.csv.expected_failures_30d  (table reports/fleet_risk_sites.csv, written by failure_model)\n  means: Fleet Health: For a site, account or the whole fleet on the scoring date: the expected number of drive failures in the next 30 days, the sum of Project 1's calibrated p_fail_30d over the drives, together with the count the Backblaze SMART rule flags. Lower expected failures per drive is healthier.\n  column path (66 upstream columns, 5 hops; the deepest 19 are in backblaze_daily_csv):\n    <- failure_model/features.p_fail_30d  [failure_model: sum(p_fail_30d) per site, rounded to 2]\n      <- failure_model/features.lightgbm  [failure_model: the calibrated lightgbm score at the fleet scoring date (score_fleet)]\n        <- failure_model/features.capacity_bytes  [failure_model: Platt-calibrated LightGBM (params in reports/failure_model_metrics.json); per-feature share is a model property (gain), not lineage]\n        <- failure_model/features.days_seen_7  [failure_model: ...]\n        <- failure_model/features.model  [failure_model: ...]\n        <- failure_model/features.smart_187_delta7  [failure_model: ...]\n           ... and 22 more at this depth\n          <- telemetry_daily.capacity_bytes  [failure_model: value at t]\n          <- telemetry_daily.date  [failure_model: smart_187_raw at t minus at t-7]\n          <- telemetry_daily.model  [failure_model: value at t; LightGBM categorical]\n          <- telemetry_daily.smart_187_raw  [failure_model: smart_187_raw at t minus at t-7]\n             ... and 15 more at this depth\n            <- backblaze_daily_csv.capacity_bytes  [load_telemetry: cast]\n            <- backblaze_daily_csv.date  [load_telemetry: cast]\n            <- backblaze_daily_csv.smart_187_raw  [load_telemetry: cast]\n            <- backblaze_daily_csv.smart_5_raw  [load_telemetry: cast]\n               ... and 15 more at this depth\n  job path:\n  <- drive_model (parquet, real_derived, by load_telemetry)\n  <- drive_summary (parquet, real_derived, by load_telemetry)\n  <- failure_model/features (dataframe, real_derived, by failure_model)\n  <- installed_asset (csv, generated_joined_to_real, by generate_enterprise)\n  <- site (csv, generated, by generate_enterprise)\n  <- telemetry_daily (parquet, real, by load_telemetry)\n  <- truth/account_resolution (csv, truth, by generate_enterprise)\n  <- truth/asset_serial_map (csv, truth, by generate_enterprise)\n    <- backblaze_daily_csv (raw_csv, real)","reading":"So the number in a site's row of the fleet-risk report is the Fleet Health term, written by `sois.failure_model`: a per-site sum of the calibrated LightGBM score, which is a function of the 25 numeric features plus the model categorical, each of which is one SMART column (or a 7-day delta or max of one) from the telemetry Parquet, which is a cast of the same column in the raw Backblaze CSV. The 66 upstream columns are the whole answer; the job path alone would say \"every input of failure_model\", which includes `site.address` and is wrong at the column level. The glossary definition rides along, which is the point of the semantic layer. A column reached by several edges (`telemetry_daily.smart_187_raw` feeds `smart_187_raw`, `_delta7` and `_max7`) is printed once, at its shortest depth, with the expression of the hop that reached it first; the graph holds all three edges.","column_query":"MATCH (c:Column {column_key: $column_key})\nMATCH p = (c)-[:DERIVED_FROM*1..12]->(up:Column)\nWITH up, p ORDER BY length(p)\nWITH up, head(collect(p)) AS p\nWITH up, length(p) AS depth, relationships(p)[-1] AS last, nodes(p)[-2] AS parent\nMATCH (up)-[:BELONGS_TO]->(t:Table)\nOPTIONAL MATCH (j:Job {job_id: last.via})\nRETURN up.column_key AS column, t.name AS table, t.source AS source, depth, parent.column_key AS parent,\n       j.name AS via, last.precision AS precision, last.expr AS expr\nORDER BY depth, column"}}